:: Shopping Menu Widget Variables [nobr]

/* To add a new color, add it to the _shopMenuColors Variable underneath giving it a unique ID.
Name is how the color will be added into the clothing library call.
Icon should be the name of the color icon inside the Shop Icons path. For unique clothing like the Contest ones, use the name of the color needed for the Add Clothing Widget to work.
>New Color model:
 { ID: , Name: , Icon:  }

To add a clothing piece to the shop, add it to the corresponding Shop Object under _shopCatalog.
Name should the the name displayed on the store, Type should be the name needed for the Add Clothing widget to work.
For colors, you can use _shopMainColors if you want the stock colors used by most clothes or an array of ID's. Even if it's just one color, it needs to be an array or else the code won't be able to access the info needed for the Icon display.
>New Clothing piece model:
 { Category: , Name: , Slot: , Type: , Price: , Colors:  },

Mitt
≽^•⩊•^≼
𝑴𝒆𝒐𝒘
*/

